    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0024" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/4–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-30T21:00:00+08:00">April 30, 1949—9
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:42 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1456. News item that British Foreign Office spokesman plans establish “friendly
                    relations” with Chinese Communist Government lends point, I believe, to mytel
                    1389, April 27, 11 a.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d9-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
